{title: Break Thou the Bread of Life}
{artist: Mary A. Lathbury / William F. Sherwin}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 110}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Book of Worship for United States Forces (Washington, DC: U.S. Government Printing Office, 1974), # 354)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Break Thou the bread of life, dear Lord, to [A]me,
[D]As Thou didst break [G]the [D]loaves be[A]side__[E7]__ the [A7]sea;
[A7]Be[D]yond [Em]the [D]sacred page [A]I [E]seek Thee, [A7]Lord;
[D]My Spirit [Em]pants [G]for Thee, O [A7]living [D]Word!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Bless Thou the truth, dear Lord, to me, to [A]me,
[D]As Thou didst bless [G]the [D]bread by [A]Ga__[E7]__li[A7]lee;
[A7]Then [D]shall [Em]all [D]bondage cease, [A]all [E]fetters [A7]fall;
[D]And I shall [Em]find [G]my peace, my [A7]all in [D]all.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Thou art the bread of life, O Lord, to [A]me,
[D]Thy holy Word [G]the [D]truth that [A]sav__[E7]__eth [A7]me;
[A7]Give [D]me [Em]to [D]eat and live [A]with [E]Thee a[A7]bove;
[D]Teach me to [Em]love [G]Thy truth, for [A7]Thou art [D]love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]O send Thy Spirit, Lord, now unto [A]me,
[D]That He may touch [G]my [D]eyes, and [A]make__[E7]__ me [A7]see:
[A7]Show [D]me [Em]the [D]truth concealed [A]with[E]in Thy [A7]Word,
[D]And in Thy [Em]Book [G]revealed I [A7]see the [D]Lord.
{end_of_verse}
